{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/10926-demonic-pacts-and-duration","id":10926,"title":"Demonic pacts and Duration","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-14T17:22:44-08:00","id":10926,"title":"Demonic pacts and Duration","content":"So, I'm gearing up to start a Demon game, and the question came up of how patch jobs work. And I realized I'm not entirely sure how the cover experiences gained from the Cover benefit in a pact interact with the Duration of the pact. If a Cover pact is signed with the duration of, say, a month, and two cover experiences are awarded, and the demon spends them together with another cover experience towards purchasing a low-level patch-job, what happens when the month is up? Are the cover experiences recalled, and what happens if they're spent in the interim, especially if, in this example, the trait purchased was only partially purchased with the spent experiences? That possibility seems like a little more bookkeeping than I'd prefer. Alternatively, are Cover pacts automatically Permanent pacts, and if so, do they have to be paid as such? Or do the cover experiences last beyond the duration of the pact?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-14T17:58:14-08:00","id":10946,"title":"","content":"Personally, I would rule that, regardless of how a character gets Cover Beats/Experiences, once awarded they are permanent. That's just how I'd do it, though, if you're looking for a page citation I don't know that there is one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-15T00:18:51-08:00","id":11096,"title":"","content":"I'm also a bit confused about the pact rules.<br /> <br /> - It is stated &quot;When combining aspects, two lesser aspects combine into a medial, and two medial (or a lesser and a medial) become a greater aspect.&quot; However, in the examples the costs for the aspects are just added, which would be much easier.<br /> <br /> - If a pact favors the human, there are no additional costs for the demon. This means, a single pact could give a human extremely powerful bonusses (We are talking about +3 to all skills, for example). In contrast, a pact in favor of the demon is in fact a disadvantage for the demon, because of the higher cost. A demon could easily outweigh the additional cost by giving the human more bonusses, without any disadvantage for the demon. Is this really intended? Or did I misunderstand something?<br /> <br /> - Duration: Are pacts by default permanent, and can be made temporary? The text under &quot;Duration&quot; implies that. However, the text under the bullet &quot;permanent&quot; says that &quot;most pacts for any kind of meaningful \u201cpatch jobs\u201d are of permanent duration on the demon\u2019s side&quot;, which implies that they require 3 points for the &quot;permanent&quot; duration. The example implies the same, since in both cases a duration aspect is added to the pact on the demon's side. For Ezra's pact: how long do the bonusses for Jessica last? Are they permanent or will they expire after a year? How long would they last without a duration aspect?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1125,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1125-gflash","user":"gflash","date":". 11-15-2013, 03:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1125-gflash","name":"gflash","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1125_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-20T20:20:09-08:00","id":15079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>gflash</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/10926-demonic-pacts-and-duration?p=11096#post11096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm also a bit confused about the pact rules.<br /> <br /> - It is stated &quot;When combining aspects, two lesser aspects combine into a medial, and two medial (or a lesser and a medial) become a greater aspect.&quot; However, in the examples the costs for the aspects are just added, which would be much easier.<br /> <br /> - If a pact favors the human, there are no additional costs for the demon. This means, a single pact could give a human extremely powerful bonusses (We are talking about +3 to all skills, for example). In contrast, a pact in favor of the demon is in fact a disadvantage for the demon, because of the higher cost. A demon could easily outweigh the additional cost by giving the human more bonusses, without any disadvantage for the demon. Is this really intended? Or did I misunderstand something?<br /> <br /> - Duration: Are pacts by default permanent, and can be made temporary? The text under &quot;Duration&quot; implies that. However, the text under the bullet &quot;permanent&quot; says that &quot;most pacts for any kind of meaningful \u201cpatch jobs\u201d are of permanent duration on the demon\u2019s side&quot;, which implies that they require 3 points for the &quot;permanent&quot; duration. The example implies the same, since in both cases a duration aspect is added to the pact on the demon's side. For Ezra's pact: how long do the bonusses for Jessica last? Are they permanent or will they expire after a year? How long would they last without a duration aspect?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd probably houserule that even imbalance in favor of the human costs extra, at least after a certain point - otherwise, the Demon can churn out ridiculously potent (for mere mortal) lackeys with huge cult followings pretty fast without much effort.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1096-squidheadjax","name":"squidheadjax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1096_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-20T22:23:14-08:00","id":15129,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>gflash</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/10926-demonic-pacts-and-duration?p=11096#post11096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- Duration: Are pacts by default permanent, and can be made temporary? The text under &quot;Duration&quot; implies that. However, the text under the bullet &quot;permanent&quot; says that &quot;most pacts for any kind of meaningful \u201cpatch jobs\u201d are of permanent duration on the demon\u2019s side&quot;, which implies that they require 3 points for the &quot;permanent&quot; duration. The example implies the same, since in both cases a duration aspect is added to the pact on the demon's side. For Ezra's pact: how long do the bonusses for Jessica last? Are they permanent or will they expire after a year? How long would they last without a duration aspect?</div> </div> </div> </div>I am not a writer, but what I got here is that every pact has to have a duration; a day or week is free but anything beyond that boosts the Demon's total. The part that talks about how almost all pacts default to permanent is less about how it works mechanically and more noting that demons usually pay the price to make it permanent. And I can't imagine that the benefits would last longer than the pact.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-20T23:50:59-08:00","id":15180,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kirby Jerusalem</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/10926-demonic-pacts-and-duration?p=15129#post15129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am not a writer, but what I got here is that every pact has to have a duration; a day or week is free but anything beyond that boosts the Demon's total. The part that talks about how almost all pacts default to permanent is less about how it works mechanically and more noting that demons usually pay the price to make it permanent. And I can't imagine that the benefits would last longer than the pact.</div> </div> </div> </div>I got that impression too.<br /> <br /> It also makes sense, if the demon's going to ask for a longer term, that they should be expected to sweeten the deal, I think. Even if what they're removing is seen by the target as doing them a favor, they're still asking (whatever actually enforces Pacts) to tweak the world for a longer term.<br /> <br /> I'd definitely still like some guidance on the questions in the OP. Also the effect of different pact lengths for the parties on the cost.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1096-squidheadjax","name":"squidheadjax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1096_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T03:41:06-08:00","id":15280,"title":"","content":"Yeah... all of your cultists getting +3 to everything, above the skill caps, too? There really should be a mechanical incentive to balance the pacts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T04:21:27-08:00","id":15296,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kirby Jerusalem</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/10926-demonic-pacts-and-duration?p=15129#post15129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am not a writer, but what I got here is that every pact has to have a duration; a day or week is free but anything beyond that boosts the Demon's total.</div> </div> </div> </div>Initally, I got that impression, too. However, one of the example pacts has no duration given, and also no information about how long it lasts. Since the mentioned pact is about establishing a cult, a short duration would not make sense. That is what still confuses me.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yeah... all of your cultists getting +3 to everything, above the skill caps, too? There really should be a mechanical incentive to balance the pacts. </div> </div> </div>I don't think all cultists get the pact benefits, only those who made a pact with the demon (so in most cases the cult leader(s)). But Since the demon can make as many pacts as he likes, he could generate an unstoppable army with superhuman skills...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1125-gflash","name":"gflash","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1125_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T04:33:04-08:00","id":15299,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>gflash</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/10926-demonic-pacts-and-duration?p=15296#post15296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think all cultists get the pact benefits, only those who made a pact with the demon (so in most cases the cult leader(s)). But Since the demon can make as many pacts as he likes, he could generate an unstoppable army with superhuman skills...</div> </div> </div> </div>Assuming he wants to keep up with the paperwork. :P<br /> <br /> But yeah, a one time cost with no increase for putting it way in favor of the human can making spamming super-cultists a significant issue.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T04:44:35-08:00","id":15306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kirby Jerusalem</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/10926-demonic-pacts-and-duration?p=15299#post15299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But yeah, a one time cost with no increase for putting it way in favor of the human can making spamming super-cultists a significant issue.</div> </div> </div> </div>Although this could easily turn against the demon...<br /> <br /> If I were a demon, I would try not to give my cultists too much power. However, if another random human has something I really want, i'd offer him whatever she wants, considering I probably will never see her again.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1125-gflash","name":"gflash","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1125_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T06:08:31-08:00","id":15326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>strider1276</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/10926-demonic-pacts-and-duration?p=10946#post10946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I would rule that, regardless of how a character gets Cover Beats/Experiences, once awarded they are permanent. That's just how I'd do it, though, if you're looking for a page citation I don't know that there is one.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think we specifically mention this, but you're correct.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T08:22:21-08:00","id":15395,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>gflash</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/10926-demonic-pacts-and-duration?p=11096#post11096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm also a bit confused about the pact rules.<br /> <br /> - It is stated &quot;When combining aspects, two lesser aspects combine into a medial, and two medial (or a lesser and a medial) become a greater aspect.&quot; However, in the examples the costs for the aspects are just added, which would be much easier.<br /> <br /> - If a pact favors the human, there are no additional costs for the demon. This means, a single pact could give a human extremely powerful bonusses (We are talking about +3 to all skills, for example). In contrast, a pact in favor of the demon is in fact a disadvantage for the demon, because of the higher cost. A demon could easily outweigh the additional cost by giving the human more bonusses, without any disadvantage for the demon. Is this really intended? Or did I misunderstand something?<br /> <br /> - Duration: Are pacts by default permanent, and can be made temporary? The text under &quot;Duration&quot; implies that. However, the text under the bullet &quot;permanent&quot; says that &quot;most pacts for any kind of meaningful \u201cpatch jobs\u201d are of permanent duration on the demon\u2019s side&quot;, which implies that they require 3 points for the &quot;permanent&quot; duration. The example implies the same, since in both cases a duration aspect is added to the pact on the demon's side. For Ezra's pact: how long do the bonusses for Jessica last? Are they permanent or will they expire after a year? How long would they last without a duration aspect?</div> </div> </div> </div>1) I think you're right. That &quot;combining aspects&quot; line may have been something left over from the initial pact rules (which were more involved). We'll fix that. <br /> <br /> 2) Yes. Demons can grant mortals a great deal of power. Of course, as with any decision a demon makes that decision needs to carry the question, &quot;Is this going to get me God-Machine'd?&quot;<br /> <br /> 3) Pacts are <i>usually</i> permanent (and would carry the +3 on the demon's side to allow for that). If you don't put in a duration aspect, it lasts a day. I think we probably should have said that soul pacts are permanent, full-stop, unless the pact is destroyed before it's enacted (in which case the mortal suffers the loss of whatever he was given, and the demon is just out a Willpower dot). <br /> <br /> Temporary pacts are tricky, I admit, because you get Experiences out of them. My inclination is that Experiences should be permanent, as Rose has said, but the text implies otherwise. We'll make sure this works and is clear before press-time.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T09:47:03-08:00","id":15439,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the clarification. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3) Pacts are <i>usually</i> permanent (and would carry the +3 on the demon's side to allow for that). If you don't put in a duration aspect, it lasts a day. I think we probably should have said that soul pacts are permanent, full-stop, unless the pact is destroyed before it's enacted (in which case the mortal suffers the loss of whatever he was given, and the demon is just out a Willpower dot). </div> </div> </div>For the given example pact between Ezra and Jessica, this means that Jessica's benefits will also last for a year (or until the written pact itself gets destroyed)?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1125-gflash","name":"gflash","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1125_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T15:36:39-08:00","id":15680,"title":"","content":"Actually, while not strictly a duration question, this seems as good place as any to ask... if a demon makes a soul pact with someone and says &quot;You've got a decade and then I'm coming for you,&quot; or putting some similar time frame on it, are they held to that? Can they come and collect (or trade the soul pact to another demon who then comes and collects) without having to wait the theoretical decade?<br /> <br /> (Y'know, I could theoretically see a demon putting a 'minimum wait' timeframe on their end of a pact to reduce the 'value' of their side of it.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Christopher Shaffer, freelancer. Game line contributions: W20, Night Horrors, TC: \u00c6on, Scion (details <a href=\"http://mythicfoxwrites.blogspot.com/2019/07/stuff-ive-worked-on.html\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>) <br /> <a href=\"http://mythicfoxwrites.blogspot.com/2020/10/actual-play-index.html\" target=\"_blank\"> <b>Blog post write-ups of my gaming sessions; Currently running Exalted, and also updating old Promethean sessions</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/171-mythicfox","name":"MythicFox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar171_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T19:17:27-08:00","id":15797,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/10926-demonic-pacts-and-duration?p=15395#post15395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1) I think you're right. That &quot;combining aspects&quot; line may have been something left over from the initial pact rules (which were more involved). We'll fix that.<br /> <br /> 2) Yes. Demons can grant mortals a great deal of power. Of course, as with any decision a demon makes that decision needs to carry the question, &quot;Is this going to get me God-Machine'd?&quot;<br /> <br /> 3) Pacts are <i>usually</i> permanent (and would carry the +3 on the demon's side to allow for that). If you don't put in a duration aspect, it lasts a day. I think we probably should have said that soul pacts are permanent, full-stop, unless the pact is destroyed before it's enacted (in which case the mortal suffers the loss of whatever he was given, and the demon is just out a Willpower dot).<br /> <br /> Temporary pacts are tricky, I admit, because you get Experiences out of them. My inclination is that Experiences should be permanent, as Rose has said, but the text implies otherwise. We'll make sure this works and is clear before press-time.</div> </div> </div> </div>So can we conclude that the Pact's section is going to get some rewording and editing before the PDF is released to us? As I've been kinda interest to see what you guys are editing before we even get the &quot;first edition&quot; pdf. So far there's the editing out of the &quot;God Machine kills baby's&quot; paragraph an alteration to On the Mend and now a clarification and edit of the pact's section. <br /> <br /> Anything else the devs have mentioned is going to be altered before the pdf comes out?<br /> <br /> Combined with inevitable proof read by over a thousand people, the &quot;corrected&quot; or &quot;second edition&quot; PDF for this game might be the tightest Onyx Path has ever released.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T23:08:27-08:00","id":15917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/10926-demonic-pacts-and-duration?p=15797#post15797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Combined with inevitable proof read by over a thousand people, the &quot;corrected&quot; or &quot;second edition&quot; PDF for this game might be the tightest Onyx Path has ever released.</div> </div> </div> </div>I had the same thought. Having the whole community proof reading books is a great idea. When I saw the near-finished PDF in the Kickstarter, I was really astonished... the whole text, for free? I really hope it works out for them, and that there are not too many people not buying the book or pdf because they think they have all they need now.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1125-gflash","name":"gflash","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1125_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-22T04:47:47-08:00","id":16048,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>gflash</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/10926-demonic-pacts-and-duration?p=15917#post15917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I had the same thought. Having the whole community proof reading books is a great idea. When I saw the near-finished PDF in the Kickstarter, I was really astonished... the whole text, for free? I really hope it works out for them, and that there are not too many people not buying the book or pdf because they think they have all they need now.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know how putting the text pdf up has either helped or hindered the books initial &quot;sales&quot; on Kickstarter. Considering its nearly a 100K and its still got 20 days to go. I think its doing fine. At current I reckon it will bottom out at 120K which would make it the 3rd most successful Kickstarter Onyx Path have ever run, with W20 and Exalted beating it. <br /> <br /> In the case of Mummy (and I believe most books released as via traditional means this year) the PDF is released. Shortly after a new thread appears on the appropriate forum and people start pointing out mispellings, format errors, missing text, unclear text, missing content etc. After which the devs go back and add it, the layout people fix any layout issues it gets reindexed (if that's necessary) and then its released as a &quot;final&quot; version PDF again. <br /> <br /> Due to the 99% text PDF Demon is already getting a certain amount of this treatment from the fan base. However, as Rose said in another thread, they are not taking all corrections at this time because they don't have the final indexed version of the text yet. Its much easier to edit when you have indexed page numbers and you know that layout won't change again. So that's why I believe they are only editing things that the fans point out as &quot;major&quot; issues such as On the Mend and now the pact language ambiguity stuff. Everything else will have to wait until be get the full indexed pdf. <br /> <br /> Though I am curious what else they might correct before the book comes out. The editing of content (namely the baby killing) seems to have been something decided before the KS even started. While the pact stuff and embed stuff is obviously the result of feedback from the fans. Hence my question to Matt about if he was going to edit/reword anything else before we see the full pdf.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-22T07:36:59-08:00","id":16104,"title":"","content":"The &quot;Dead Babies&quot; sidebar had actually already been edited out, it's just that the text that Rose used to make the &quot;preview edition&quot; on the KS predated that. But otherwise, here's what I know we're tweaking: <br /> <br /> 1) On the Mend<br /> 2) Temporary Pacts (just to clarify some things, no major changes)<br /> 3) Adding in Experience costs for Cover (to clarify, BTW, it's 3 Cover Experiences to buy a dot of Cover)<br /> <br /> I can't <i>think</i> of anything else, but there's still lots of time left in the KS (HINT HINT TELL YOUR FRIENDS).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-23T03:10:34-08:00","id":16550,"title":"","content":"Also, has it been clarified whether buying a dot of Primum at character creation is supposed to be 3 or 5 Merit dots (as per page 125 of the PDF)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Christopher Shaffer, freelancer. Game line contributions: W20, Night Horrors, TC: \u00c6on, Scion (details <a href=\"http://mythicfoxwrites.blogspot.com/2019/07/stuff-ive-worked-on.html\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>) <br /> <a href=\"http://mythicfoxwrites.blogspot.com/2020/10/actual-play-index.html\" target=\"_blank\"> <b>Blog post write-ups of my gaming sessions; Currently running Exalted, and also updating old Promethean sessions</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/171-mythicfox","name":"MythicFox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar171_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-23T06:36:42-08:00","id":16606,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MythicFox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/10926-demonic-pacts-and-duration?p=16550#post16550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, has it been clarified whether buying a dot of Primum at character creation is supposed to be 3 or 5 Merit dots (as per page 125 of the PDF)?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes that would be nice to pin down before the final PDF is out. Could that become number 4 on your list Matt?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-23T23:35:48-08:00","id":16966,"title":"","content":"Where is this idea coming from that it'd be 5 merit dots for a second dot of [Insert Supernatural Attribute Here]? Did I miss a developer stating that somewhere?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;Seven deadly sins/Seven ways to win/Seven holy paths to hell/And your trip begins/Seven downward slopes/Seven bloodied hopes/Seven are your burning fires/Seven your desires&quot; \u2014 Iron Maiden,</i> Moonchild","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1122-the-grim-lich","name":"The Grim Lich","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-24T03:46:26-08:00","id":17067,"title":"","content":"1 Merit dot is equal to 1xp. Each dot of a Power Stat (Blood Potency, Gnosis, Primum, etc) cost 5xp. Ergo, a dot of a Power Stat cost the same as 5 dots of Merits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-24T03:56:17-08:00","id":17069,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Grim Lich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/10926-demonic-pacts-and-duration?p=16966#post16966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where is this idea coming from that it'd be 5 merit dots for a second dot of [Insert Supernatural Attribute Here]? Did I miss a developer stating that somewhere?</div> </div> </div> </div>The idea came from the notes of Rose about Blood and Smooke","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-24T07:59:53-08:00","id":17120,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/10926-demonic-pacts-and-duration?p=17067#post17067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1 Merit dot is equal to 1xp. Each dot of a Power Stat (Blood Potency, Gnosis, Primum, etc) cost 5xp. Ergo, a dot of a Power Stat cost the same as 5 dots of Merits.</div> </div> </div> </div>But under the old XP system, 3 merit dots could be wildly divergent in XP cost from 1 dot of a Power Stat. You could have used those 3 dots to buy 3 1-dot merits (6 XP) or you could have used them to buy the third and fourth dots of one merit and the third dot of a different merit (20 XP), whereas the cost of the second dot of [Power Stat] was fixed at 16 XP. In fact, there aren't a lot of ways you can use 3 out of 7 free merit dots to add up to equal to or more than one dot of [Power Stat]. It's going to, generally, cost <i>less</i> for those three merit dots than it did for the dot of [Power Stat] that you sacrificed those three merit dots for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;Seven deadly sins/Seven ways to win/Seven holy paths to hell/And your trip begins/Seven downward slopes/Seven bloodied hopes/Seven are your burning fires/Seven your desires&quot; \u2014 Iron Maiden,</i> Moonchild","edited":{"userid":1122,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1122-the-grim-lich","user":"The Grim Lich","date":".  Edited for clarification 11-24-2013, 11:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1122-the-grim-lich","name":"The Grim Lich","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-24T14:11:35-08:00","id":17299,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Grim Lich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/10926-demonic-pacts-and-duration?p=17120#post17120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But under the old XP system, 3 merit dots could be wildly divergent in XP cost from 1 dot of a Power Stat. You could have used those 3 dots to buy 3 1-dot merits (6 XP) or you could have used them to buy the third and fourth dots of one merit and the third dot of a different merit (20 XP), whereas the cost of the second dot of [Power Stat] was fixed at 16 XP. In fact, there aren't a lot of ways you can use 3 out of 7 free merit dots to add up to equal to or more than one dot of [Power Stat]. It's going to, generally, cost <i>less</i> for those three merit dots than it did for the dot of [Power Stat] that you sacrificed those three merit dots for.</div> </div> </div> </div>The cost of a six-dot Merit is only two experience points higher than the cost of the first two new dots of Supernatural Tolerance. The cost of a three-dot Merit is four experience points lower than the cost of the first new dot of Supernatural Tolerance. Both of those rates are the highest-priced experience costs those Merit dots could save you without tossing around fragmentary portions.<br /> <br /> A difference of two to four experience points doesn't even out to a difference of two Experiences. One, perhaps, but definitely not two.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-24T20:55:27-08:00","id":17491,"title":"","content":"A difference of ten experience points, on the other hand, <i>does</i> even out to a difference of two experiences. Which is what my &quot;3 1-dot merits&quot; example would be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;Seven deadly sins/Seven ways to win/Seven holy paths to hell/And your trip begins/Seven downward slopes/Seven bloodied hopes/Seven are your burning fires/Seven your desires&quot; \u2014 Iron Maiden,</i> Moonchild","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1122-the-grim-lich","name":"The Grim Lich","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-24T21:04:35-08:00","id":17494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Grim Lich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/10926-demonic-pacts-and-duration?p=17491#post17491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A difference of ten experience points, on the other hand, <i>does</i> even out to a difference of two experiences. Which is what my &quot;3 1-dot merits&quot; example would be.</div> </div> </div> </div>I fail to see in what universe this is a cogent argument. &quot;The difference is big if you compare buying ST up to the absolute lowest experience-point-value use of those Merit dots&quot; does the opposite of support the notion that keeping the price at three starting Merit dots is a sensible assumption. At no point is anyone going to argue that a dot of Supernatural Tolerance is worth the same as three one-dot Retainers.<br /> <br /> For the record, you wanted a citation, and <a href=\"http://forums.white-wolf.com/default.aspx?g=posts&amp;m=1685963#post1685963\" target=\"_blank\">here it is:</a><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>machineiv</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">FWIW, in B&amp;S, Blood Potency costs 5 of your starting Merit dots, per level. But you get 10 Merits. So yeah.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://forums.white-wolf.com/default.aspx?g=posts&amp;m=1665741#post1665741\" target=\"_blank\">Another for good measure:</a><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>machineiv</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, the cost of Blood Potency goes up to five of your Merit dots (since they cost five Experiences, it's equal cost). So, you can spend all ten to get BP 3.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://forums.white-wolf.com/default.aspx?g=posts&amp;m=1624072#post1624072\" target=\"_blank\">And tic-tac-toe:</a><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>machineiv</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, it brings Blood Potency in line with one of my design goals for GMC: to make everything cost the same, no matter when you buy it. Blood Potency is five Experiences, which is the same as five Merits. So, five Merits will net you a Blood Potency at creation.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 11-25-2013, 12:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-25T07:28:12-08:00","id":17689,"title":"","content":"Oh, see, I'd not seen those. Hmm. <br /> <br /> I like it better as 3 of your starting Merit dots, though I do see David's point. Let me consult with Rose and David and we'll see.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-26T08:35:35-08:00","id":18422,"title":"","content":"Yep, 5 Merit dots for Primum at chargen. <br /> <br /> Also: Slight change to the rules for temporary pact duration (and yes, this is going to change in the text of the game). If you do a pact which is a) temporary and b) uses Cover as the reward for the demon, you get a transient, one-effective-dot Cover. It's not really Cover; you can't use it to go loud, there's not enough fuel there to burn, as it were. It's kind of the equivalent of wearing a false mustache or another simple disguise. Useful so that you can do some recon or whatever without exposing your &quot;real&quot; Cover.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-26T08:43:58-08:00","id":18425,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/10926-demonic-pacts-and-duration?p=18422#post18422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yep, 5 Merit dots for Primum at chargen.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good to know.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/10926-demonic-pacts-and-duration?p=18422#post18422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also: Slight change to the rules for temporary pact duration (and yes, this is going to change in the text of the game). If you do a pact which is a) temporary and b) uses Cover as the reward for the demon, you get a transient, one-effective-dot Cover. It's not really Cover; you can't use it to go loud, there's not enough fuel there to burn, as it were. It's kind of the equivalent of wearing a false mustache or another simple disguise. Useful so that you can do some recon or whatever without exposing your &quot;real&quot; Cover.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oooooh, that's neat. I like that.<br /> <br /> Also, if I may reiterate my question from earlier without getting smacked on the nose by a newspaper...<br /> <br /> If a demon makes a soul pact with someone and says &quot;You've got a decade and then I'm coming for you,&quot; or putting some similar time frame on it, are they held to that? Can they come and collect (or trade the soul pact to another demon who then comes and collects) without having to wait the theoretical decade?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Christopher Shaffer, freelancer. Game line contributions: W20, Night Horrors, TC: \u00c6on, Scion (details <a href=\"http://mythicfoxwrites.blogspot.com/2019/07/stuff-ive-worked-on.html\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>) <br /> <a href=\"http://mythicfoxwrites.blogspot.com/2020/10/actual-play-index.html\" target=\"_blank\"> <b>Blog post write-ups of my gaming sessions; Currently running Exalted, and also updating old Promethean sessions</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/171-mythicfox","name":"MythicFox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar171_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-26T08:46:28-08:00","id":18427,"title":"","content":"Are you still 100% ok with people giving out high rewards on the mortal side to keep the pact balanced for the Demon? It just seems...open to abuse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-26T09:42:42-08:00","id":18469,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/10926-demonic-pacts-and-duration?p=18422#post18422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also: Slight change to the rules for temporary pact duration (and yes, this is going to change in the text of the game). If you do a pact which is a) temporary and b) uses Cover as the reward for the demon, you get a transient, one-effective-dot Cover. It's not really Cover; you can't use it to go loud, there's not enough fuel there to burn, as it were. It's kind of the equivalent of wearing a false mustache or another simple disguise. Useful so that you can do some recon or whatever without exposing your &quot;real&quot; Cover.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really like those paper-thin Covers and plan to collect a bunch, given the chance, haha. Do they still count toward your maximum amount of Covers, dictated by Primum?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/478-intrepid-vector","name":"Intrepid Vector","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar478_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-26T11:00:42-08:00","id":18510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/10926-demonic-pacts-and-duration?p=18422#post18422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yep, 5 Merit dots for Primum at chargen. Also: Slight change to the rules for temporary pact duration (and yes, this is going to change in the text of the game). If you do a pact which is a) temporary and b) uses Cover as the reward for the demon, you get a transient, one-effective-dot Cover. It's not really Cover; you can't use it to go loud, there's not enough fuel there to burn, as it were. It's kind of the equivalent of wearing a false mustache or another simple disguise. Useful so that you can do some recon or whatever without exposing your &quot;real&quot; Cover.</div> </div> </div> </div> This brings new and terrible meanings to using sometime as a &quot;beard&quot;. Bravo, sir.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1096-squidheadjax","name":"squidheadjax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1096_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}